      summary:
        '<p><strong>Microsoft Corp.</strong> today released software updates to plug at least 570 security holes in its <strong>Windows</strong> operating systems and other software, almost triple the number of vulnerabilities the software giant fixed in its record-smashing Patch Tuesday release last month. Microsoft attributed the burgeoning patch counts to vulnerability discoveries aided by artificial intelligence.</p>\n<p><img decoding="async" class=" wp-image-56287 aligncenter" src="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/windupate.png" alt="A picture of a windows laptop in its updating stage, saying do not turn off the computer." width="749" height="527" srcset="https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/windupate.png 841w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/windupate-768x541.png 768w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/windupate-782x550.png 782w, https://krebsonsecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/windupate-100x70.png 10',
      sourceUrl:
        "https://krebsonsecurity.com/2026/07/microsoft-patches-a-record-570-security-flaws/",
